<h3 class="wp-block-heading">An Invitation</h3>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">There are substantial risks to this endeavor: persuasive bad arguments, accelerated error, conformity, unwarranted deference, and assistance to harmful projects. Visible reasoning may itself invite excessive trust. Critical involvement must include studying these failures and identifying where reliance is unwarranted. We also need to assess the environmental costs of scaling and its effects on access, research priorities and human philosophical expertise.&nbsp;&nbsp;</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">The work we need from philosophers is substantial philosophy that contributes to our evaluation and benchmark development. Develop a stronger argument, a better interpretation, a distinction that changes what follows in an important case, or an account of how several arguments contribute jointly to a conclusion. Help determine what warrants a probability assigned to a philosophical premise, or how an inquiry should respond when an interpretation is corrected. These contributions could shape the engine’s methods, becoming demanding reference work, and inform the inquiries delivered to users. We welcome sustained collaborators, potential cofounders, research partnerships and, as funding allows, paid specialist contributions. The work should advance contributors’ own research as well as the system.&nbsp;</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">We also welcome arguments against this conception of philosophical inquiry and against developing or deploying systems intended to realize it.&nbsp;</p>



